From a895dc572296f1ced17e533335d4bc4d16d5d80d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GuaiYiHu <guaiyihu@foxmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 03:03:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] bpf: Select truthful Android 17 network capabilities on
 opted-in 3.4 products

Adapt the current Android17 loader and program metadata for the actual Aries/MiOne ARM32 network backport. Require product/build opt-in, the real 3.4 kernel and no kver_override. Retain all actual required map/program/BTF, attach/query, completion and verifier failures. Probe actual versions rather than compiler-assumed minimums for these builds.

Include the implemented mmapable arrays, LRU, socket storage, ring buffers, boot time, socket lookup/release and cgroup socket release. Select current Android17 accounting, local-network protection, loopback checks, tracing and socket-option logic with explicit truthful 3.4 metadata. Keep unsupported 6.1-only TCPAccECN and 5.15 bind-return features outside the profile.

Validation: 15 BPF objects compile with current Soong BPF flags; default code and runtime metadata match the fixed Android17 baseline byte-for-byte. All 19 required netd programs select uniquely with complete map references and actual helper IDs. ARM32 KernelUtils compiles with/without the profile. Host ASan/UBSan replay of the actual Aries verifier core with modeled context/helper callbacks accepts the 22 selected ELF programs. These are compile and host-harness results, not actual Android17 device verifier/JIT/network validation. Full Android17 loader/netd compilation remains a separate gate.
Change-Id: Id870ffe5a8de444363853b2f54d8c825cb8d6b29
